pkg/fanal/analyzer is imported by every part of the scan pipeline, and it
imported pkg/iac/detection for eleven string constants and pkg/misconf for
the type of one option field. Those two edges alone linked the whole IaC and
misconfiguration stack: Helm and the Kubernetes client, Terraform and
go-getter (S3, GCS, gRPC/xDS), OPA and chroma.

The constants are inlined with their values, and the misconfiguration scanner
option becomes `any`: the wrapper never enables misconfiguration scanning, so
the option is never set, and the config analyzers that read it are not
linked. pkg/cache folds the option's (always empty) check and data paths into
its cache key; it now uses the empty list directly.

